      "curatorId": "cur_ingrid-halvorsen",
      "note": "Ambient for daylight. No drone longer than the kettle takes; this is a list to do something else to.",
      "updated": "2026-08-22",
      "updatedLabel": "3 days ago"
    },
    {
      "playlistId": "pl_the-archive",
      "curatorId": "cur_ade-mensah",
      "note": "Forty tracks of Accra and Lagos crate finds. The liner notes are longer than some of the songs, on purpose.",
      "updated": "2026-08-20",
      "updatedLabel": "5 days ago"
    },
    {
      "playlistId": "pl_late-night-heat",
      "curatorId": "cur_amara-diallo",
      "note": "Made for the drive home after the drive home. Nothing here asks for your full attention until the third song, and then it takes it.",
      "updated": "2026-08-19",
      "updatedLabel": "6 days ago"
    },
    {
      "playlistId": "pl_jazz-nights",
      "curatorId": "cur_marcus-pike",
      "note": "Small rooms, late sets, the count-in left in. If you can hear the bassist breathe, it made the cut.",
      "updated": "2026-08-18",
      "updatedLabel": "1 week ago"
    },
    {
      "playlistId": "pl_cassette-dreams",
      "curatorId": "cur_haruka-nakagawa",
      "note": "Shoegaze and dream pop that still hisses. I kept the ones where the tape is part of the song, not a filter on top of it.",
      "updated": "2026-08-11",
      "updatedLabel": "2 weeks ago"
    },
    {
      "playlistId": "pl_poolside",
      "curatorId": "cur_luana-andrade",
      "note": "Cumbia, bossa, and things that move at the speed of a Sunday. Play it loud enough that the neighbours ask.",
      "updated": "2026-08-04",
      "updatedLabel": "3 weeks ago"
    },
    {
      "playlistId": "pl_tropicalia",
      "curatorId": "cur_luana-andrade",
      "note": "The Rio pressings and the Bogotá ones side by side. You can tell them apart by the hiss, and now so can you.",
      "updated": "2026-07-14",
      "updatedLabel": "14 Jul"
    },
    {
      "playlistId": "pl_string-theory",
      "curatorId": "cur_ingrid-halvorsen",
      "note": "Modern composition for strings, mostly. Two of these were recorded in the same church, eleven years apart. You can hear the roof.",
      "updated": "2026-06-28",
      "updatedLabel": "28 Jun"
    },
    {
      "playlistId": "pl_midnight-sax",
      "curatorId": "cur_marcus-pike",
      "note": "Ballads only. I put this together for a friend who couldn't sleep and it has outlived the insomnia.",
      "updated": "2026-05-09",
      "updatedLabel": "9 May"
    }
  ],
